Azure CLI Installation & VM SKU Availability Guide
Professional Step-by-Step Guide

OPTION 1 - Azure Portal (Cloud Shell)
STEP 1: Sign in
Open https://portal.azure.com and sign in with your Azure account.

STEP 2: Open Cloud Shell
Click the Cloud Shell icon from the top menu. Select Bash or PowerShell. Azure CLI is already installed.

STEP 3: Verify Subscription

az account show --output table
az account list --output table
az account set --subscription "<Subscription Name or Subscription ID>"

STEP 4: Check Standard_DS1_v2 Availability

az vm list-skus --resource-type virtualMachines --all --query "[?name=='Standard_DS1_v2' && !contains(restrictions[].reasonCode, 'NotAvailableForSubscription')].locationInfo[0].location" --output table
Note: Listed regions are not blocked for your subscription. Deployment may still fail due to quota or capacity.

STEP 5: Logout
az logout

==============================================
OPTION 2 - Local Windows Azure CLI
STEP 1: Check Azure CLI Installation

az version
Note: If 'az' is not recognized, install Azure CLI.

STEP 2: Install Azure CLI (User)

winget install -e --id Microsoft.AzureCLI --scope user

STEP 3: Install Azure CLI (Administrator)

$ProgressPreference='SilentlyContinue'; Invoke-WebRequest -Uri https://aka.ms/installazurecliwindows -OutFile AzureCLI.msi; Start-Process msiexec.exe -ArgumentList '/i AzureCLI.msi /quiet /norestart' -NoNewWindow -Wait; Remove-Item AzureCLI.msi

STEP 4: Restart & Verify
Close PowerShell, open a new window, then run:
az version

STEP 5: Login

az login

STEP 6: Verify Subscription

az account show --output table
az account list --output table
az account set --subscription "<Subscription Name or Subscription ID>"

STEP 7: Check Standard_DS1_v2 Availability

az vm list-skus --resource-type virtualMachines --all --query "[?name=='Standard_DS1_v2' && !contains(restrictions[].reasonCode, 'NotAvailableForSubscription')].locationInfo[0].location" --output table

STEP 8: Logout

az logout

STEP 9: Verify Logout

az account show

